    musicBtn: "Music folder ↗", musicT: "Songs from a folder", musicOk: "Got it", musicOpen: "Open folder", musicHtml: "<p>Your songs live in the <b>Music</b> folder next to the program — each in its own numbered folder: <code>Music\\1\\</code>, <code>Music\\2\\</code>… They show up in “{mine}” in that order.</p><ul><li><b>Easiest — the “+ {add}” button:</b> pick a file, type the artist and title — the program creates the next folder by itself.</li><li><b>Or by hand:</b> make a folder with the next number and put the song file (mp3, flac, wav, ogg, m4a) and a picture for the cover (jpg, png) into it. No picture — we draw a cover.</li><li><b>Picture:</b> any name if it's the only one in the folder; if there are several — <code>cover.jpg</code> is used (or the one named like the mp3). Any size: in the game the cover is 256×256, a non-square one is cropped to the center.</li><li>Artist and title come from the mp3 tags or the file name; to fix them — the pencil ✎ on the song.</li><li>The race start (GO) and the finish are set automatically. To check — click the song.</li><li>Delete a folder from Music — the song disappears from the program too. To change the order — rename the folders.</li></ul>", musicImpT: "Songs from Music", musicStep: "{n} of {m}: {a}", musicAdded: "Songs added: {n}. GO and finish were set automatically — check them with the pencil ✎ on a song. Then <b>{build}</b>.", musicGone: "Removed: {n} — their files are no longer in Music. <b>{build}</b> to remove them from the game too.", musicFail: "Couldn't read: {a}", delMusic: "<p>The program won't pick this song up from the Music folder again.</p>",
