    madeBy: "made by", claudeRole: "AI · code", devRole: "developer", poweredBy: "runs with", hubSub: "Your own songs in every NFS game — Unbound, Heat and the whole series", hubRole: "all NFS games", ourPages: "our pages", site: "Website", sortT: "Sort", artT: "Artist", whereSelT: "Where it plays", sortOrder: "My order", sortArtist: "Artist A→Z", sortTitle: "Title A→Z", sortNew: "Newest first", artAll: "All artists", whereAll: "Everywhere", whereRace: "RACES only", whereCity: "CITY only", whereGarage: "GARAGE only", whereLow: "LOW only", viewTiles: "Tiles", viewList: "List", prioTip: "How often it plays: HIGH — often, LOW — rarely (the game picks HIGH first). Click to change", err_orderFail: "Couldn't change the order ({a}). Close Explorer or a player that has the Music folder open and try again.", betaNote: "We keep improving the program — found a bug? <b>Report it ↗</b>", helpBtn: "How it works", helpT: "How it works", covUp: "Upload a picture", covGen: "Generate from the title", covDel: "Remove the picture", helpHtml: "<h3>Game tracks</h3><p>{legend}</p><h3>Your songs</h3><ul><li><b>+ Add song</b> — an mp3, flac, wav, ogg or m4a file. The song goes into the <b>Music</b> folder next to the program.</li><li><b>▶ From YT Music</b> — paste a link to a song, playlist or album (or drag it from the browser). If the playlist has a music video, the program takes the same song from YT Music — without the video's intros and skits. Not found — it downloads the video.</li><li><b>Music folder</b> — your whole library: folders 1, 2, 3… are the order in the program. Put in a folder with a song — it appears by itself; delete the folder — the song leaves the program too.</li><li><b>Drag & drop</b> — drop song files onto the window to add them; drag your song's card to change the order (the Music folders get renumbered; works in “My order” without filters).</li></ul><h3>View</h3><p>Tiles, small tiles or list, sort by artist / title / newest, filter by artist and where it plays. <b>HIGH / LOW</b> on a card — how often the track plays: HIGH often, LOW rarely (the game takes HIGH first).</p><p><b>RACES / CITY / GARAGE</b> — sections under “My songs” and “Game tracks”: what plays where right now. <b>+</b> next to a section — pick songs for that place; click a section header to fold / unfold it.</p><h3>Song settings — pencil ✎</h3><ul><li><b>Cover</b> — upload your picture, generate one from the title, or remove it.</li><li><b>Race start</b> — 17 s cutscene (green) + 3.45 s countdown 3-2-1 (orange), the drop hits at <b>GO</b>. Drag the GO marker onto the drop — you'll hear the countdown right away.</li><li><b>Finish</b> — the yellow block: what plays after the finish line. Drag it with the mouse.</li><li><b>RACES / CITY / GARAGE</b> — where the song plays.</li><li><b>Volume</b> — 0–300 %. <b>Auto</b> brings a quiet song up to the level of the others. <b>Overload protection</b> keeps it from crackling above 100 %; turned off — it may crackle and distort.</li></ul><h3>Profiles</h3><p>A profile is a set: which game tracks and which of your songs are on. Songs are shared: in another profile a song is simply off. Switched the profile — press “Build mod” again.</p><h3>Mod in the game</h3><ol><li><b>Build mod</b> — the program puts UnboundSoundtrack.fbmod into the Mods folder of your Frosty Mod Manager.</li><li>Frosty Mod Manager: enable <b>UnboundSoundtrack</b>, disable other music mods → <b>Launch</b>.</li><li>Play <b>offline</b>.</li></ol><h3>How many songs</h3><p>About 350 of your own songs. Disabled game tracks free up more room (up to ~389).</p><h3>Something's wrong</h3><p><b>Log</b> (bottom left) — what the program did. <b>Report a bug</b> — describe what you did and paste the end of the log.</p>", about: "Credits", log: "Log",
